# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MIRROR — NOT THE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
#
# This is a read-only copy of the silicaui host block as it exists TODAY in the
# sparx repo's unified routing table, `k8s/ingress/Caddyfile`. It already ships
# there; nothing needs to be pasted anywhere for silicaui.com to route. The copy
# lives here so this repo can explain its own ingress without a second checkout.
#
# It is deliberately NOT applied from this repo, and an in-cluster ConfigMap
# edit would be pointless: the live config is Kustomize-generated and
# hash-named, so a hand edit is overwritten on the next `kubectl apply -k`.
# To change routing, change it in the sparx repo and redeploy Caddy there.
#
# THE ON-DEMAND TLS DECISION (reversed from what this file used to say):
# an earlier version of this block omitted on-demand TLS on the theory that the
# ask endpoint would reject silicaui.com. The opposite turned out to be the
# operative constraint. Caddy runs as a SINGLE replica on a `Recreate` rollout,
# so every boot has a ~15–60s window with no registered load-balancer backend,
# and an explicit managed block fires all of its startup issuance attempts
# inside exactly that window — a FIRST certificate can never be obtained at
# boot. That cost a day. On-demand defers issuance to the first HTTPS request,
# which lands on a warm, LB-registered pod, so the ACME challenge succeeds.
# silicaui.com and www are allow-listed as static platform hosts in the ask
# endpoint (`services/api-rest/src/routes/internal/domain-check.ts`), so
# issuance is authorized. `{$SX_SCHEME:https}` and `tls_policy` are the
# Caddyfile's own portability seam — https + ACME on any cluster with a public
# IP, plain HTTP on a workstation cluster behind a tunnel.
#
# Requires silicaui.com and www.silicaui.com to resolve to the AKS ingress:
#   20.12.217.0   (pip-ingress-sparx-prod-cus, rg-sparx-prod-cus-nodes)
# kept grey-cloud / DNS-only in Cloudflare so ACME challenges reach the origin.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

{$SX_SCHEME:https}://silicaui.com {
	import tls_policy
	import security_headers
	reverse_proxy site.silicaui.svc.cluster.local:80
}

{$SX_SCHEME:https}://www.silicaui.com {
	import tls_policy
	import security_headers
	redir https://silicaui.com{uri} permanent
}
